// toolbox/appleevents.cla: curated AppleEvent Manager declarations
// (Inside Macintosh VI, "Apple Event Manager"), mac-resident-clarusc
// Task 12 -- the first System 7.1 boot (Snow emulator) found that Clarus
// apps ignore the required-suite Quit AppleEvent, so a running app blocks
// Finder shutdown until force-quit. This catalog is the minimal slice
// that fixes it: enough of the AppleEvent Manager for a program to
// install its own event handler (a `callback func`) and pump
// AEProcessAppleEvent from a real WaitNextEvent loop.
//
// Convention, and why this ISN'T `trap 0xA816 sel N` like
// toolbox/standardfile.cla's own Standard File Package routines: every
// AppleEvent Manager routine dispatches through the ONE shared trap
// 0xA816, distinguished by a selector word -- but unlike the "Package"
// trap families (Standard File's 0xA9EA, the List Manager's 0xA9E7),
// which PUSH the selector immediately before the trap
// (THREEWORDINLINE(0x3F3C, sel, trap) -- 0x3F3C is MOVE.W #sel,-(SP)),
// every AppleEvent Manager routine instead PRELOADS the selector into D0
// (THREEWORDINLINE(0x303C, sel, trap) -- 0x303C is MOVE.W #sel,D0). This
// task's own language-reference addition, the `seld0` clause (Trap and
// Inline Clauses), is exactly this second shape; `sel` cannot express it.
//
// Every trap word and selector below is confirmed directly against
// Apple's own Universal Interfaces 3.4 (Retro68/InterfacesAndLibraries/
// Interfaces), the authoritative source in this repo, per the standing
// "decode the inline words" rule (toolbox/osutils.cla's own header
// comment) -- corroborated BOTH ways (the C pragma's THREEWORDINLINE and
// the assembly macro's raw OPWORDs, which must and do agree):
//
//   AEInstallEventHandler  CIncludes/AppleEvents.h:136-142:
//               `EXTERN_API( OSErr ) AEInstallEventHandler(
//               AEEventClass theAEEventClass, AEEventID theAEEventID,
//               AEEventHandlerUPP handler, long handlerRefcon, Boolean
//               isSysHandler) THREEWORDINLINE(0x303C, 0x091F, 0xA816);`
//               -- seld0 0x091F. Corroborated in AIncludes/
//               AppleEvents.a:105-114: `_AEInstallEventHandler:
//               move.w #$091F,D0 / dc.w $A816`.
//   AEProcessAppleEvent    CIncludes/AEInteraction.h:87-95:
//               `EXTERN_API( OSErr ) AEProcessAppleEvent(const
//               EventRecord *theEventRecord) THREEWORDINLINE(0x303C,
//               0x021B, 0xA816);` -- seld0 0x021B. Corroborated in
//               AIncludes/AEInteraction.a:72-81: `_AEProcessAppleEvent:
//               move.w #$021B,D0 / dc.w $A816`.
//
// handler: a `callback func` matching AEEventHandlerUPP's own signature
// (Inside Macintosh: `pascal OSErr MyHandler(const AppleEvent
// *theAppleEvent, AppleEvent *reply, long handlerRefcon)`) -- decays to
// its glue address at the call site (language reference's `callback
// func` section), the same mechanism uitable.cla's rtUiLdefDraw/
// uitext.cla's rtUiScrollbarAction already use for an LDEF/action
// procedure. theEventRecord (AEProcessAppleEvent): the raw 16-byte buffer
// a real UiWaitNextEvent call already filled in for a kHighLevelEvent.
//
// Deliberately NOT in this minimal slice: AEGetParamDesc/AECountItems/
// AEGetNthPtr/AEDisposeDesc (decoding a kAEOpenDocuments docList into
// FSSpecs) and AEGetAttributePtr (the keyMissedKeywordAttr completeness
// check IM recommends for every handler) -- runtime/clarus/native.cla's
// own AE handler doesn't install a kAEOpenDocuments/kAEPrintDocuments
// handler at all, so the AppleEvent Manager's own built-in dispatch
// already answers both with errAEEventNotHandled with no code needed
// here; a future task can add real document-drop-while-running delivery
// (FSSpec -> path, OpenWD/SetVol) if that becomes a real requirement,
// the same way toolbox/files.cla grew its own FSSpec-adjacent entries
// incrementally. kCoreEventClass and the four required-suite event IDs
// are cataloged below regardless (CIncludes/AppleEvents.h:82-90) --
// documentation-cheap even where this task's own runtime use only
// touches two of them (oapp/quit).

const kCoreEventClass: int = 0x61657674 // 'aevt'
const kAEOpenApplication: int = 0x6F617070 // 'oapp'
const kAEOpenDocuments: int = 0x6F646F63 // 'odoc'
const kAEPrintDocuments: int = 0x70646F63 // 'pdoc'
const kAEQuitApplication: int = 0x71756974 // 'quit'

external func AEInstallEventHandler(theAEEventClass: int, theAEEventID: int, handler: ptr, handlerRefcon: int, isSysHandler: bool): word = trap 0xA816 seld0 0x091F
external func AEProcessAppleEvent(theEventRecord: ptr): word = trap 0xA816 seld0 0x021B
